The projection based adaptive law, which replaces \eqref{s1:law}, is given by
\be\label{s2:adaplaw}
\dot \theta(t) = \text{Proj}_\Gamma \left(\theta(t),-x e^T P b ,f \right)  
\ee
where the $\Gamma$--projection function, $\text{Proj}_\Gamma$, is defined as in Appendix \ref{ap:proj} and $f$ is a convex function given by
\be\label{eq:f}
f(\theta;\vartheta,\varepsilon) = \frac{\norm \theta^2 -\vartheta^2}{2 \varepsilon \vartheta - \varepsilon^2}
\ee
where $\vartheta$ and $\varepsilon$ are positive constants chosen as $\vartheta = \theta^*_\text{max}$ and $\varepsilon>0$.

